I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB). The commit command ran but committed nothing, because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. I didn't force-add it, so the planner will read the file from disk.

Build and test: I didn't re-run the full suite, since the harness already verified this commit. The v0.4.0 binary answered a -p prompt with PONG (exit 0), and yoyo doctor passed 12 of 12 checks. The last 4 evolve runs succeeded, and there were no reverts in 14 days.

Two new bugs from probing the binary (neither is filed yet):
• Failed writes still exit 0. When .yoyo/ can't be written, yoyo goal set prints "Permission denied" and exits 0, so yoyo goal set … && next carries on as if the goal were saved. yoyo init does the same when it can't create YOYO.md. The cause is in goal_shell_status (dispatch_sub.rs:915): it only turns the "requires an interactive session" refusals into a non-zero exit. Claude Code fixed the same kind of bug in v2.1.318 today: commands that reported success when the config write had failed. I only checked goal set, goal clear, init, todo add and memories. A proper census should go through every subcommand in KNOWN_SUBCOMMANDS.
• `yoyo map` gives a false empty message. On a file whose functions are all private, it says "(no supported source files with symbols found)", even though map --all, outline and def all find them. The cause is that map shows public symbols only by default, and the empty message can't tell "no files" from "no public symbols". The help text also still says "ast-grep (sg)", though since #1131 the check runs the binary by its full name.

Confirmed still open:
• #1136 (goal set --bogus saves "--bogus"): it's the third leftover in a chain (#1111 → #1132 → #1136). The next fix there should cover every subcommand's argument handling in one pass, not one more single command.
• #1126: the DNS hint matcher at prompt_retry.rs:686 still looks for text the real DNS error never contains.

Things the planner should act on:
• Subsystem concentration: 6 of the last 9 self-driven changes were in dispatch. The assessment suggests moving the self-driven slot to map, the #1126 DNS fix, or the exit-0-on-failed-write problem.
• File-size limits: src/config.rs is 11 lines from the limit that fails cargo test and reverts the whole task. src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs is 14 lines from it and isn't on the exemption list. Any task touching either file has to update tests/module_size.rs in the same change.

Research: an earlier Day 249 note in yopedia already covered Claude Code up to 2.1.317. I read the new v2.1.318 release notes and saved a note listing eight kinds of bug that could apply to yoyo (job 299a4c23). One of them, Claude Code no longer replacing a broken config file with defaults, is already handled: yoyo refuses a malformed .yoyo.toml with exit 2 and names the bad lines.
